 support of John  MacDonald Lisa Nandi is seen as a strong  voice for the north of the country but  would she win the backing of Pro Corbin  members Angela Rayner has also been  talked up by Mr Macdonald as a future  leader part of the new blood of the  party  he has helped to foster Jess Phillips on  the other hand would be seen as a big  departure from the current leadership  but she worries the Tories which should  in theory  please labor both saki-sama and Emily  Thornbury are experienced and signed up  to mr corbyn's politics but are they too  tied to the old regime  the reality is Labour's next leader will  be chosen by the very movement mr. cool  been set up will those members be  willing to turn away from the project  they helped build some Labour MPs hope  they might the battle for the house of  the party has already turned nasty with  recriminations flying about the way the  leadership treated voters in the north  caroline flint speaking earlier today  about emily Thornbury she said to one of  my colleagues I'm glad my constituents  aren't as stupid as yours I'm sorry it's  not acceptable a claim denied by Miss  Thornbury who said this is a title and  utter lie I have never said this to  anyone nor anything like it and I hope  needless to say not something I would  ever think whoever leads labour out of  the Corbin years faces a battle to hold  on to remain backing city seats while  regaining the heartlands which voted to  leave and they'll do it in the shadow of  a conservative prime minister who still  can't believe his luck and is determined  to hold on to those hard-won votes  Kate McCann Sky News
 

